/F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 2: Cassel Rock Light) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -32 Td
(Cassel Rock Light sits on a bare island two kilometres offshore. It was built in 1867) Tj 0 -16 Td
(after the steamer Lady Ondine sank on the rock with the loss of 63 lives. The tower) Tj 0 -16 Td
(is painted with red and white horizontal bands so that it can be recognised in) Tj 0 -16 Td
(daylight. Its light shows a steady red beam. Because the rock is often cut off by) Tj 0 -16 Td
(heavy seas, keepers were supplied by a basket hauled along a cable from the mainland.) Tj 0 -16 Td
(The longest recorded isolation lasted 47 days in the winter of 1903, when the keepers) Tj 0 -16 Td
(survived on salted fish and rainwater.) Tj 0 -16 Td
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 296 40 Td (Page 3) Tj ET
endstream
