/F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 3: Marrowind Lantern) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -32 Td
(The Marrowind Lantern is the smallest light in the bay, only 9 metres tall. It was) Tj 0 -16 Td
(built in 1889 from cast iron prefabricated in a foundry at Glasmere and shipped in) Tj 0 -16 Td
(214 numbered pieces. It marks the narrow channel into the inner harbour and shows a) Tj 0 -16 Td
(green light that flashes once every three seconds. The lantern was the first in the) Tj 0 -16 Td
(region to be converted to electricity, in 1921. Its keeper, Ada Fenwick, was the) Tj 0 -16 Td
(first woman appointed as a principal keeper on this coast, and she served from 1921) Tj 0 -16 Td
(until her retirement in 1950.) Tj 0 -16 Td
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 296 40 Td (Page 4) Tj ET
