BT
/F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 5: Automation and the Bay Today) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
0 -32 Td
(All five lighthouses were automated between 1979 and 1994. Hollin Point was the last) Tj 0 -16 Td
(to lose its keepers, on 30 June 1994. The lights are now monitored remotely from a) Tj 0 -16 Td
(control room in the town of Saltmere, and solar panels power the Marrowind Lantern) Tj 0 -16 Td
(and Cassel Rock Light. The Merrow Bay Lighthouse Trust maintains the keepers') Tj 0 -16 Td
(cottages and runs guided walks along the 23-kilometre coastal path that links the) Tj 0 -16 Td
(four mainland lights. Tickets for the boat trip to Cassel Rock must be booked in) Tj 0 -16 Td
(advance because landings depend on the tide.) Tj 0 -16 Td
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 296 40 Td (Page 6) Tj ET
